# The repo-wide `*.jsonl` rule exists to keep training corpora out of the
# tree. These are not corpora: they are hand-written EVALUATION cases with
# expected fields, no real traffic rows, and a metric ships with the thing
# that produces it -- an uncommitted scorer is how v6's calibration numbers
# became unreproducible.
#
# Run OUTPUT is not here at all: benchmark.py writes to --output, which the
# README points at /tmp. So there is nothing in this directory to ignore
# except bytecode, which the repo-wide rule already covers.
!cases.jsonl
!tool_cases.jsonl
!tool_cases_v1.jsonl
